[  10.3s]   ✅ Saturation result:   I(X-fibre) : c^∞   =   I(P-fibre).
[  10.3s]      Combined with fibre dim = 2 at all 5 sampled generic A points,
[  10.3s]      and the c=0 component collapsing to V (where (α,β) ≡ (0,0)),
[  10.3s]      we have the full decomposition:
[  10.3s] 
[  10.3s]         X  =  P  ∪  X_{c=0}      (set-theoretic, over a generic A)
[  10.3s]         X_{c=0}  ⊆  R^12 × V × {0}      ⇒ image in Q is {0}.
[  10.3s] 
[  10.3s]      ⇒  Every (A, A', c) ∈ X with c ≠ 0 has A' = (α·λ, β·μ).
[  10.3s]         Every (A, A', c) ∈ X with c = 0 has (α(A'), β(A')) = (0, 0).
[  10.3s] 
[  10.3s]      IMPOSSIBILITY THEOREM (unconditional, char-0 fields):
[  10.3s]      Suppose three rank-1 atoms (L_k·M_k)_{k=1..3} have pairwise-
[  10.3s]      proportional garbages.  For each pair (k, k') either
[  10.3s]        (a) c_{k,k'} ≠ 0  and  L_{k'} = α·L_k, M_{k'} = β·M_k, OR
[  10.3s]        (b) c_{k,k'} = 0  and one of the two atoms has (α, β) = (0, 0).
[  10.3s]      In case (a) the (α_k, β_k) projections of the pair lie on one
[  10.3s]      line in Q; in case (b) one atom contributes 0 to Q.  Either way,
[  10.3s]      the three (α_k, β_k) span at most a 1-dim subspace of Q ≅ R^2,
[  10.3s]      so they cannot simultaneously realise T1 and T2 mod S.
[  10.3s] 
[  10.3s]      ⇒ No 3-atom (2,2,bridge-3) construction exists in the rank-1
[  10.3s]        atom family over any field of characteristic 0.
